  "scope": "Two unrelated source hosts move the actual waiting parent Vm twice while original Seq/All saved collector rows are parked, then restore via existing native admission. Twelve mixed programs cover atoms, Seq/All/expanded repeat, group captures, successors and a second group. Original lexical buffers, shared group owners, accepted reply buffers and outstanding work are retained; output, fuel, request counts and invocations match uninterrupted LocalVm at every budget cutoff. Stale root receipts return intact. Every checkpoint tests closed scope, revoked grants, stale identity, wrong root and capture-site refusal; injected native admission unwind is tested at first, middle and final boundaries. The fixture explicitly owns and closes ScopedLocalExecution<Option<Vm>>; no new public helper, automatic external cancellation, arbitrary native cleanup fence, durable transaction or complete extraction claim is added.",
